cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use The Daily Me in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Daily Me: an open-source personal newspaper written by AI"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Udotai
    given-names: Joshua C.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-10"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/romanthegentle/daily-me"
keywords:
  - personalized news
  - news recommendation
  - large language models
  - AI agents
  - filter bubble
abstract: >-
  The Daily Me builds a personal newspaper every morning. A reader profile says who the
  reader is and what they follow. For each section, a Claude reporter searches and reads
  the web, then files sourced articles in its own words; an editor composes the front page.
  Editions skip stories the reader has already seen, and each one carries a story from
  outside the reader's interests to work against the filter bubble.
